&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;The gaming industry is larger than movies, music, and books combined, with over 3 billion active gamers playing monthly and over 25 million active developers worldwide. Mobile gaming, in particular, is the fastest-growing segment, projected to reach $300 billion by 2025. At Skillz, you have the opportunity to be at the forefront of this exciting industry and shape its future.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;06ede768&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;This role owns retention economics, LiveOps incentive efficacy (CPIN), the payment funnel, and virtual-economy/matchmaking policy for Skillz&#39;s India platform business, from Bangalore. Incentive spend against a ~$40M pool only compounds retention and NGR when it&#39;s held to a CPIN discipline — incentive $ per incremental NGR $ vs. a randomized holdout — rather than just tracked after the fact. It also owns the retention plan itself and represents finance directly in Product&#39;s roadmap for owned titles, so retention economics shape what gets built rather than just measuring it after the fact. As the only seat in this structure with a formal direct report (FP&amp;amp;A Analyst — LiveOps), this role also carries people-management accountability: setting that analyst&#39;s KPIs, coaching their development, and ensuring incentive-efficacy work scales across titles without funneling every decision through Head of Finance.&lt;/p&gt;
